The old executable put back over a database a newer release migrated.

1. Release 5 renames `title`.
2. Release 6 fixes rows (a step) and changes no table.
3. Release 5 again: its ledger is the start of the database's, and
   schema.sql is what the database holds: it opens as it is, and the
   database still records release 6's step.
4. Release 7 adds a column.
5. Release 5 again: refused, rather than drop the column.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup');

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== ledger
ALTER TABLE dish RENAME COLUMN title TO name;

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== ledger
ALTER TABLE dish RENAME COLUMN title TO name;
UPDATE dish SET name = upper(name);

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== ledger
ALTER TABLE dish RENAME COLUMN title TO name;

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, note TEXT) STRICT;

== ledger
ALTER TABLE dish RENAME COLUMN title TO name;
UPDATE dish SET name = upper(name);

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== ledger
ALTER TABLE dish RENAME COLUMN title TO name;

